<p>&#8220;Ethel administers necessary discipline to Archie and Quentin.&#8221; Theodore Roosevelt drew this picture of three of his children <a href="https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.111519/page/n117/mode/2up">on White House stationery</a> in 1904. Ethel would have been 12, Archie 10, and Quentin 6.</p>
<p>Roosevelt wrote elsewhere, &#8220;I don&#8217;t think that any family has ever enjoyed the White House more than we have.&#8221;</p>
